  "methodology_notes": "Public SDK refresh review, 2026-10-17\nVersions: OVRTX 0.6.0.1791947691; OVStage 0.3.0.1791986420; Newton 1.7.0; URDF converter 0.3.4. Warp 1.18.0, USD Core 26.8, USD Exchange 3.0.1 and USD validation 1.22.0 are already current public direct dependencies.\nOVRTX 0.6 requires OVStage 0.3. The application constructs PathDictionary with the owning stage, creates a fresh stage when opening USD, uses lane-based writes with explicit float64 matrix shape, and does not consume changed read/map attribute layouts. No API patch was identified from those changes; native Linux validation remains mandatory.\nNewton 1.7 removes scalar gravity; application already constructs the axis-specific gravity vector. It does not use ModelBuilder.add_urdf, so URDF damping mode change is not a runtime path. Existing local USD assets remain unchanged with original converter provenance. No MPM or neural checkpoint feature is enabled.\nLinux native validation held: worker root 98% full (~10 GiB available), /dev/shm and user runtime tmpfs 100% full. Fresh isolated SDK installation must wait for sufficient space or another qualified worker. No cleanup or mount changes were performed.\nFramework admission still blocked by target-specific dependency scanning (literate-ai issue 65). No source filtering/import aliases or gate bypass added.\n"
